# =============================================================================
# StackFund — Hermes model credentials.
#   PASTE YOUR KEY, then:  cp docker/agent.env.example docker/agent.env
#   (docker/agent.env is git-ignored. The run scripts copy it to
#    .hermes-data/.env — the file Hermes actually reads at /opt/data/.env.)
#
# Set EXACTLY ONE provider block below (the provider auto-detects from the key).
# Do NOT put inline `# comments` after a KEY=value line.
#
# Hackathon requires a Hermes model → use Option 1, or Option 3 pointed at a
# Hermes-serving endpoint.
# =============================================================================

# --- Option 1: Nous Portal (Hermes; simplest) --------------------------------
# Get a key: `hermes portal open` or https://portal.nousresearch.com
# Confirm model ids with `hermes model --refresh` (Hermes-4-70B/-405B/-14B).
NOUS_API_KEY=
HERMES_INFERENCE_MODEL=Hermes-4-70B

# --- Option 2: Anthropic (Claude) — native API -------------------------------
# To use this instead, comment out Option 1 above and uncomment these:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# HERMES_INFERENCE_MODEL=claude-opus-4.6

# --- Option 3: OpenAI-compatible endpoint ------------------------------------
# OpenAI / OpenRouter / vLLM / Ollama / self-hosted Hermes-4. The provider
# auto-detects "openai" from OPENAI_API_KEY; OPENAI_BASE_URL points at the host.
# To use this instead, comment out Option 1 above and uncomment these:
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# HERMES_INFERENCE_MODEL=NousResearch/Hermes-4-70B

# --- OPTIONAL: Stripe earn/spend (SANDBOX test key) --------------------------
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=rk_test_...
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...

# --- OPTIONAL: dashboard on :9119 --------------------------------------------
# HERMES_DASHBOARD=1
